GAP J-W001-A | ring main board J_BAND_A land 1 (UP), face F.Cu; tail land on F.Cu, to FLEX1 tail land 1 (JOY_UP); hot bar (main board land to FLEX1 tail land 1), every ring size US 7 to 13 | waits for hotbar-joint.md (process.md P8 change C17): solder: band-interface.md asks a pre-tinned board land (stencil paste 0.05 mm or a tinned land), but no step tins it: step 2 gives the land no paste, step 4 cleans it to bare copper, step 16 adds none; ring-F_Paste.gbr holds no opening at this land (logs/probe_paste.log); the tail land is bare ENIG; no file read here names a 0.05 mm stencil (review 3 G1) ; orientation: step 16 holds the board parts face up while the tail arrives with its lands face up (band-interface.md section 3), so the lands cannot meet unless the board faces down or the tail turns; no file read here says which (review 3 G3) ; alignment: the fixture with the 0.10 mm outline is drawn in no file (review 3, fixture-search.log) and the ring board has no silkscreen; nothing says how to set the foot on the 0.51 mm pitch (review 3 G3) ; heat (note): 260 C, 4 s, 20 N are the band builder's starting values, and the same line gives the Alps and polyimide limit as 260 C 3 s; step 16 of the guide carries no heat value ; check: nothing checks this FLEX1 land at step 16 (band-interface.md section 7 asks continuity 'by the test pads', but none of the 12 test pads of step 5 carries this net); the first proof is T-JOY and T-CENTRE at step 18, after step 17 closes the joint for good
